# Drafted by Gemini (R24 will), edited.

~ marianna
Narrator: Damp straw and lantern smoke hang in the stable yard as you hold Alda's folded parchment out to the stablemistress.
marianna_grey [afraid]: That is Mrs. Farnum's wax seal, sure enough. Why would you bring her private papers out here to the horses, unless there is some mistake?
* Read it to her -> read_it
* Give her the will -> deliver
* [ends:alda_will] Burn the will and say nothing -> burn
* Keep it, say nothing for now -> END

~ read_it
Narrator: She rests her palm flat against an old mare's warm neck while you read out the bequest of the Green Queen Inn, its keys, and its ledgers.
marianna_grey [sad]: All of it left to me, even the cellars and the debt. I only ever swept the cobbles and minded her greys when the nights turned frost.
-> marianna

~ deliver
Narrator: Her chapped fingers tremble as she takes the heavy parchment and tucks it beneath her wool shawl.
marianna_grey [weary]: I will keep the doors open the same way I keep these stalls, quiet and clean, with dry bedding and no hard words.
take alda_will
set alda_will_delivered
quest alda_will delivered
standing patient_lady +1
-> after

~ after
marianna_grey [smile]: First thing I do is light the kitchen grate and put a hot pan of mutton and oats in front of Jean and Siv.
-> END

~ burn
Narrator: While Marianna turns to latch a stall door, you feed the parchment into the stable lantern until the wax, the ink, and the inn's old debts curl into black ash.
take alda_will
quest alda_will burned
-> END
